    {
      "heading": "The lead changes hands",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "social-2110031207601979715",
        "person-yi-chia-chen-identity-0",
        "person-dries-smit-identity-0"
      ],
      "text": "Tufa Labs closes the evening ARC-AGI-3 public board first at 68.91, ahead of Yi-Chia Chen at 67.49. The gap is 1.42 points. The recorded overnight event took Tufa from 56.52 and second place to the lead; Chen’s score is unchanged against the previous evening boundary. ARC Prize publicly confirmed Tufa’s return to first today. This is a team result: the fresh Tufa roster lists dlorah, driessmit1, infinitecreativity, jeroencottaar, pressman1 and stefano1283."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Vineeth makes the top ten",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "wire-2026-10-13-0756-arc-3-vineeth-sai-varikuntla-enters-gold",
        "social-2109599257980555583"
      ],
      "text": "Vineeth Sai Varikuntla gains 5.75 points against the previous evening comparison, climbing from 32nd to ninth at 40.09. That is a consequential move into the leading group, rather than merely keeping pace with a growing field. 復活の混テキスト holds 39.53 in tenth: PunkCyber’s team remains in the top ten even after slipping one place."
    },
    {
      "heading": "NVARC3 is a team",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "social-2109971877091274960",
        "person-jean-francois-puget-identity-0",
        "person-darragh-hanley-identity-0",
        "person-elad-sarafian-identity-0",
        "person-gal-kaplun-identity-0",
        "person-ivan-sorokin-identity-0",
        "person-yeyin-zhu-identity-0"
      ],
      "text": "NVARC3 stands fourth at 43.94, just ahead of the last dance 🕺 at 43.64; mtg is third at 45. An observed NVARC3 score event rose from 40.97 to 43.94, but its previous-evening net comparison is unavailable. Jean-François Puget reminded the paper today that NVARC is a team. The six currently listed NVARC3 accounts map to Puget, Darragh Hanley, Elad Sarafian, Gal Kaplun, Ivan Sorokin and Yeyin Zhu. The score belongs to that entry; the roster does not identify who produced a submission."
    },
    {
      "heading": "The medal line keeps moving",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "wire-2026-10-13-1557-arc-3-tom-enters-gold",
        "wire-2026-10-13-0605-arc-3-daniel-franzen-climbs-to-25th",
        "person-daniel-franzen-identity-0"
      ],
      "text": "The afternoon wire caught Tom. jumping from 1,135th to 17th at 37.18 in its observed window. Tonight’s gold-score threshold is 37.12, up from 36.98 at the previous evening snapshot. Lord Han Solo’s unchanged 36.98 now sits 20th. Daniel Franzen is 27th at 35.86, unchanged against this edition’s baseline: the morning wire’s gain came from an earlier rolling comparison and should not be counted again as an evening gain. Public medal positions remain provisional."
    },
    {
      "heading": "A separate harness result",
      "sourceIds": [
        "social-2110060578530001231"
      ],
      "text": "Away from the Kaggle race, ARC Prize announced a DeepSeek V4.1 Flash evaluation at about 3% with a provider adapter and under 1% with its standard harness. The linked organizer results compare low reasoning for the former headline result with max reasoning for the latter. That distinction matters when interpreting the comparison; it is a separate model evaluation and establishes no method behind today’s leading Kaggle teams."
    }
